>> title: Collard Greens, Instant Pot
>> category: Stews & Braises
>> tags: greens, southern, pork, side, instant pot, pressure cooker
>> counters: Instant Pot
>> dish: collard-greens
>> kit: Instant Pot
>> aka: greens, collards, turnip greens, mustard greens, mixed greens, pot likker, potlikker, instant pot collard greens, pressure cooker collards
>> pairs-with: ham-hock-stock, skillet-cornbread, hot-water-cornbread, black-eyed-peas
>> servings: 6
>> time: 1 hr
>> slack: narrow — it is vented the second the timer ends, because greens go from done to collapsed inside a natural release
>> step.2: trim the ribs out, wash in three waters
>> step.3: render 8 min
>> step.4: sweat 6 min
>> step.5: 20 min high pressure, quick release
>> step.6: season at the very end

Two cups of stock and not three quarts. The greens give up their own water and the pot keeps all of it.

Trim @collard greens{3%lb}(1.4 kg; thick ribs pulled out, leaves cut in wide ribbons) and wash them in three changes of water until no grit settles.

Render @thick-cut bacon{6%slices}(chopped) on sauté in an #Instant Pot{} for ~render{8%min}.

Sweat @&(~1)bacon{} with @yellow onion{1%large}(diced), @garlic{4%cloves}(sliced) for ~sweat{6%min}.

Pressure cook @&(~1)pork base{}, @&(~3)washed greens{} with @ham hock stock{2%cup}(475 mL), @cider vinegar{2%Tbs}, @light brown sugar{1%tsp}, @crushed red pepper{1/2%tsp} — the greens packed down in handfuls, lid on and valve sealed: ~come to pressure{10%min}, then ~pressure cook{20%min} on high and ~quick release{2%min}, standing clear of the valve.

Season @&(~1)greens{} with @kosher salt{2%tsp}, @black pepper{1%tsp}, @hot sauce{1%Tbs}, and pour the liquid left in the pot into a cup to send out beside them.
